        h3 Education
        link edit /w/index.php?title=Languages_of_Kyrgyzstan&action=edit&section=2
      text Following the 2005 , educational reforms in 2007 required that Kyrgyz become a required subject in non-Kyrgyz-language schools, and that Russian become a required subject in schools with a language of instruction other than Russian.
      link "Tulip Revolution" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulip_Revolution
      link [6] #cite_note-:0-6
      row
        h2 Minority languages
        link edit /w/index.php?title=Languages_of_Kyrgyzstan&action=edit&section=3
      text is spoken by approximately 850 thousand residents of Kyrgyzstan and is the second most spoken native language, ahead of Russian and behind Kyrgyz.
